    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575-a1">

                <pb facs="0959" n="889" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg889"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 298.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Dufferin to Mr. Heap.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Therapia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 27,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Heap</hi>: I am informed unofficially
                    that the ministry have recommended the dismissal both of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">vali</hi> of Bitlis and of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >vali</hi> of Van.</p>
                <p>I have been looking through the instructions I have sent to our consul-general.
                    Colonel Everett, and both Mr. Wyndham and I consider that they will enable him
                    to give your missionaries the assistance they desire.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DUFFERIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
